{"id": "fixed-crews-fixed-stations", "title": "Fixed crews, fixed stations: what the fire staffing rules lock in", "seconds": 142.7, "voice": "elevenlabs:iPYqcpY8j8Ap4jUf28I3", "narrator": "Michael", "tempo": 1.2, "made": "2026-11-24", "key": "89050ed783fcbc92", "words": 394, "beats": [{"scene": "open", "kind": "slam", "ref": ["story[4]", "established[3]", "established[4]"], "text": "Do the City’s fire rules require wooden ladders?", "t0": 0.2, "t1": 3.25, "shot": "b0", "visual": {"type": "slam", "words": ["Wooden", "ladders?"], "sub": "and a second driver at the back of a truck"}, "emph": ["wooden ladders"], "wt": [0.0, 0.15, 0.27, 0.7, 1.06, 1.42, 1.86, 2.14]}, {"scene": "open", "kind": "slam", "ref": ["story[4]", "established[4]"], "text": "Or a second driver at the back of a truck?", "t0": 3.25, "t1": 6.25, "shot": "b0", "visual": {"type": "slam", "words": ["Wooden", "ladders?"], "sub": "and a second driver at the back of a truck"}, "wt": [0.04, 0.19, 0.25, 0.54, 0.9, 1.01, 1.11, 1.35, 1.44, 1.51]}, {"scene": "open", "kind": "count", "ref": ["established[3]", "story[4]"], "text": "Wooden ladders: not found in 458 agreement texts, or 300 code sections.", "t0": 6.25, "t1": 12.22, "shot": "b1", "visual": {"type": "count", "value": "458", "label": "agreement text files searched: no wooden ladders", "sub": "nor in 300 Charter and code sections"}, "emph": ["not found"], "wt": [0.04, 0.44, 1.33, 1.64, 1.99, 2.12, 2.42, 2.72, 3.24, 3.62, 4.54, 4.68, 4.91, 5.16, 5.44]}, {"scene": "open", "kind": "bignum", "ref": ["suspicious[4]", "established[4]"], "text": "The second driver exists. It’s the tiller operator, and it’s paid extra.", "t0": 12.34, "t1": 16.78, "shot": "b2", "visual": {"type": "bignum", "value": "60", "label": "tiller positions on 20 trucks", "sub": "paid a 5% premium"}, "emph": ["tiller operator"], "wt": [0.0, 0.13, 0.42, 0.77, 1.78, 2.01, 2.11, 2.42, 3.27, 3.47, 3.67, 4.01]}, {"scene": "open", "kind": "caveat", "ref": ["caveat"], "text": "This is a lead, not a finding.", "t0": 16.9, "t1": 18.57, "shot": "b3", "visual": {"type": "caveat", "line": "This is a lead, not a finding: a pattern in public records. This film says what the records show, what they do not show, and what would settle it."}, "wt": [0.0, 0.19, 0.33, 0.4, 0.99, 1.17, 1.24]}, {"scene": "lead1", "kind": "form", "ref": ["suspicious[0]", "links[3]"], "text": "The first lead: the firefighters’ agreement fixes the crews.", "t0": 18.79, "t1": 22.08, "shot": "b4", "visual": {"type": "form", "title": "Firefighters’ agreement, section 22.1", "sub": "The first lead", "rows": [["Engine", "1 officer + 3 firefighters"], ["Truck", "1 officer + 4 firefighters"], ["Truck, aerial ladder out", "1 officer + 5 firefighters"]]}, "wt": [0.0, 0.11, 0.39, 1.14, 1.28, 1.87, 2.29, 2.68, 2.77]}, {"scene": "lead1", "kind": "form", "ref": ["suspicious[0].what", "story[1]"], "text": "One officer and three on an engine. One and four on a truck.", "t0": 22.2, "t1": 25.71, "shot": "b4", "visual": {"type": "form", "title": "Firefighters’ agreement, section 22.1", "sub": "The first lead", "rows": [["Engine", "1 officer + 3 firefighters"], ["Truck", "1 officer + 4 firefighters"], ["Truck, aerial ladder out", "1 officer + 5 firefighters"]]}, "emph": ["four on a truck"], "wt": [0.0, 0.2, 0.61, 0.78, 1.12, 1.23, 1.33, 2.11, 2.4, 2.58, 2.95, 3.06, 3.14]}, {"scene": "lead1", "kind": "quote", "ref": ["suspicious[0].what", "established[0]"], "text": "The truck clause is in all 5 full agreement texts since 2018.", "t0": 25.83, "t1": 29.7, "shot": "b5", "visual": {"type": "quote", "line": "All trucks shall be regularly and routinely staffed with one (1) officer and four (4) firefighters", "kicker": "In 5 of 5 full agreement texts since 2018"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.11, 0.36, 0.73, 0.85, 0.97, 1.22, 1.53, 1.7, 2.06, 2.78, 3.04, 3.32]}, {"scene": "lead1", "kind": "clock", "ref": ["suspicious[0].why"], "text": "Every seat is filled each watch, on overtime if need be.", "t0": 29.82, "t1": 32.56, "shot": "b6", "visual": {"type": "clock", "hours": 24, "label": "every seat, every watch", "sub": "filled by a regular member, or someone on overtime"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.27, 0.49, 0.61, 0.92, 1.19, 1.57, 1.75, 2.15, 2.27, 2.46]}, {"scene": "lead2", "kind": "doc", "ref": ["suspicious[1]", "links[0]"], "text": "The second lead: Proposition F keeps every 2004 firehouse and apparatus in service.", "t0": 32.78, "t1": 39.61, "shot": "b7", "visual": {"type": "doc", "kicker": "Budget and Legislative Analyst, January 2014", "text": "This legislation permanently locked into place the City’s 2004 emergency response system", "mark": "permanently locked into place"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.17, 0.57, 1.45, 2.22, 2.81, 3.16, 3.5, 3.8, 4.26, 4.53, 5.09, 5.19, 6.05, 6.28]}, {"scene": "lead2", "kind": "doc", "ref": ["suspicious[1].what", "established[1]", "links[6]"], "text": "In 2014, the Budget and Legislative Analyst wrote it permanently locked that system in.", "t0": 39.73, "t1": 44.56, "shot": "b7", "visual": {"type": "doc", "kicker": "Budget and Legislative Analyst, January 2014", "text": "This legislation permanently locked into place the City’s 2004 emergency response system", "mark": "permanently locked into place"}, "emph": ["permanently locked"], "wt": [0.0, 0.12, 0.4, 1.24, 1.37, 1.62, 1.74, 2.23, 2.85, 3.1, 3.23, 3.75, 4.0, 4.16, 4.52]}, {"scene": "lead2", "kind": "bignum", "ref": ["suspicious[1].what", "story[2]", "established[1]"], "text": "The daily minimum: 297.", "t0": 44.68, "t1": 48.06, "shot": "b8", "visual": {"type": "bignum", "value": "297", "label": "daily suppression minimum, 2014", "sub": "3.44 full-time posts for each daily seat"}, "emph": ["297"], "wt": [0.0, 0.14, 0.47, 1.15, 1.46, 1.85]}, {"scene": "lead2", "kind": "bignum", "ref": ["suspicious[1].what", "story[2]", "established[1]"], "text": "Each seat takes 3.44 full-time posts to fill.", "t0": 48.06, "t1": 51.96, "shot": "b8", "visual": {"type": "bignum", "value": "297", "label": "daily suppression minimum, 2014", "sub": "3.44 full-time posts for each daily seat"}, "wt": [0.04, 0.35, 0.93, 1.23, 1.58, 1.87, 2.15, 2.44, 2.97, 3.47, 3.59]}, {"scene": "lead3", "kind": "versus", "ref": ["suspicious[2]", "established[2]", "links[7]"], "text": "The third lead. In 2004, the Controller compared truck crews with other cities.", "t0": 52.48, "t1": 58.11, "shot": "b9", "visual": {"type": "versus", "a": ["San Francisco, Milwaukee, San Jose", "5 on a truck"], "b": ["The five remaining jurisdictions", "4 on a truck"], "kicker": "Controller, 2004"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.2, 0.7, 1.81, 1.97, 2.16, 2.54, 3.18, 3.32, 3.77, 4.16, 4.43, 4.82, 4.98, 5.2]}, {"scene": "lead3", "kind": "versus", "ref": ["suspicious[2].what", "established[2]"], "text": "Like San Francisco, Milwaukee and San Jose put five on a truck.", "t0": 58.23, "t1": 61.34, "shot": "b9", "visual": {"type": "versus", "a": ["San Francisco, Milwaukee, San Jose", "5 on a truck"], "b": ["The five remaining jurisdictions", "4 on a truck"], "kicker": "Controller, 2004"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.15, 0.31, 0.79, 1.29, 1.39, 1.62, 2.04, 2.26, 2.62, 2.73, 2.8]}, {"scene": "lead3", "kind": "versus", "ref": ["suspicious[2].what", "established[2]"], "text": "The five remaining cities all used four.", "t0": 61.46, "t1": 63.39, "shot": "b9", "visual": {"type": "versus", "a": ["San Francisco, Milwaukee, San Jose", "5 on a truck"], "b": ["The five remaining jurisdictions", "4 on a truck"], "kicker": "Controller, 2004"}, "emph": ["four"], "wt": [0.0, 0.13, 0.39, 0.75, 1.08, 1.29, 1.55]}, {"scene": "lead3", "kind": "quote", "ref": ["suspicious[2].what", "suspicious[2].why", "timeline[0]"], "text": "It urged new approaches to fixed staffing. No later comparison is on disk.", "t0": 63.51, "t1": 67.91, "shot": "b10", "visual": {"type": "quote", "line": "The Department should consider new approaches to fixed staffing and to response modes", "kicker": "Controller, 2004"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.17, 0.59, 0.76, 1.32, 1.45, 1.72, 2.72, 3.0, 3.28, 3.78, 3.9, 4.04]}, {"scene": "lead4", "kind": "line", "ref": ["suspicious[3]", "trajectory"], "text": "The fourth lead: overtime of the four ranks that fill those crews.", "t0": 68.13, "t1": 71.5, "shot": "b11", "visual": {"type": "line", "series": [0], "kicker": "Overtime, fire crew ranks H-2, H-3, H-20, H-30", "from": "FY2014", "to": "FY2026"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.13, 0.42, 1.12, 1.65, 1.72, 1.82, 2.07, 2.31, 2.45, 2.68, 2.89]}, {"scene": "lead4", "kind": "bignum", "ref": ["suspicious[3].what", "amount", "links[4]"], "text": "57.4 million dollars in fiscal 2026.", "t0": 71.62, "t1": 75.76, "shot": "b12", "visual": {"type": "bignum", "value": "$57.4 million", "label": "overtime, crew ranks, fiscal 2026", "sub": "$38.9 million in fiscal 2014"}, "emph": ["57.4 million"], "wt": [0.0, 0.79, 1.04, 1.33, 1.78, 2.61, 2.8, 3.15, 3.41]}, {"scene": "lead4", "kind": "bignum", "ref": ["suspicious[3].what", "amount", "links[4]"], "text": "38.9 million in fiscal 2014.", "t0": 76.18, "t1": 79.04, "shot": "b12", "visual": {"type": "bignum", "value": "$57.4 million", "label": "overtime, crew ranks, fiscal 2026", "sub": "$38.9 million in fiscal 2014"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.6, 0.9, 1.22, 1.58, 1.69, 2.01, 2.26]}, {"scene": "lead4", "kind": "scene", "ref": ["suspicious[3].why", "story[3]", "notEstablished[1]"], "text": "That overtime also covers absences, vacancies and injuries. The payroll doesn’t say which.", "t0": 79.46, "t1": 84.64, "shot": "b13", "visual": {"type": "scene", "art": "question", "label": "Not the rule alone", "sub": "absences, vacancies, injuries, deployments"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.18, 0.69, 0.97, 1.28, 1.98, 2.6, 2.76, 3.68, 3.85, 4.3, 4.59, 4.8]}, {"scene": "lead4", "kind": "doc", "ref": ["established[6]", "suspicious[3].why"], "text": "The same 2014 audit found overtime can cost less than filling vacant posts.", "t0": 84.76, "t1": 89.46, "shot": "b19a", "visual": {"type": "doc", "kicker": "Budget and Legislative Analyst, January 2014", "text": "overtime can be less costly than permanent positions when paid time off and fringe benefits are factored into the position costs", "mark": "less costly"}, "emph": ["cost less"], "wt": [0.0, 0.13, 0.47, 0.76, 1.21, 1.54, 1.79, 2.66, 2.84, 3.18, 3.42, 3.57, 3.86, 4.16]}, {"scene": "lead4", "kind": "bignum", "ref": ["established[7]", "suspicious[3].why"], "text": "And the State’s 2025 pay file ranks San Francisco’s fire overtime share 13th of 14.", "t0": 89.58, "t1": 95.56, "shot": "b19b", "visual": {"type": "bignum", "value": "13th of 14", "label": "San Francisco’s fire overtime share, State Controller’s pay file, 2025", "sub": "23.7% of regular pay; middle of the others 42.2%"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.13, 0.24, 0.63, 0.88, 1.4, 1.64, 1.97, 2.22, 2.44, 3.02, 3.86, 4.52, 4.82, 5.35, 5.44]}, {"scene": "lead5", "kind": "scene", "ref": ["suspicious[4]", "story[4]"], "text": "The fifth lead: the second driver.", "t0": 95.78, "t1": 97.59, "shot": "b14", "visual": {"type": "scene", "art": "van", "label": "The tiller operator", "sub": "the second driver, at the back of a truck", "kicker": "The fifth lead"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.2, 0.54, 0.96, 1.13, 1.43]}, {"scene": "lead5", "kind": "scene", "ref": ["established[4]", "story[4]"], "text": "Those words appear in none of 3,133 documents.", "t0": 97.71, "t1": 103.33, "shot": "b14", "visual": {"type": "scene", "art": "van", "label": "The tiller operator", "sub": "the second driver, at the back of a truck", "kicker": "The fifth lead"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.38, 0.74, 1.1, 1.24, 1.6, 1.7, 2.05, 2.62, 2.84, 3.55, 4.38]}, {"scene": "lead5", "kind": "scene", "ref": ["established[4]", "story[4]"], "text": "The job is the tiller operator.", "t0": 103.33, "t1": 105.13, "shot": "b14", "visual": {"type": "scene", "art": "van", "label": "The tiller operator", "sub": "the second driver, at the back of a truck", "kicker": "The fifth lead"}, "wt": [0.04, 0.25, 0.66, 0.8, 0.92, 1.28]}, {"scene": "lead5", "kind": "form", "ref": ["suspicious[4].what", "links[5]"], "text": "The agreement pays tiller operators a 5 percent premium.", "t0": 105.25, "t1": 107.96, "shot": "b15", "visual": {"type": "form", "title": "Section 28.1, apparatus operator pay", "sub": "2026 vacancy list", "rows": [["Tiller operator premium", "5% of base"], ["Tiller positions", "60 on 20 trucks"]]}, "emph": ["5 percent"], "wt": [0.0, 0.15, 0.54, 0.83, 1.14, 1.6, 1.69, 1.93, 2.26]}, {"scene": "lead5", "kind": "form", "ref": ["suspicious[4].what", "story[4]"], "text": "The 2026 vacancy list shows 60 tiller positions on 20 trucks.", "t0": 108.08, "t1": 112.35, "shot": "b15", "visual": {"type": "form", "title": "Section 28.1, apparatus operator pay", "sub": "2026 vacancy list", "rows": [["Tiller operator premium", "5% of base"], ["Tiller positions", "60 on 20 trucks"]]}, "wt": [0.0, 0.13, 0.43, 0.98, 1.43, 1.99, 2.31, 2.73, 3.01, 3.45, 3.57, 3.84]}, {"scene": "lead5", "kind": "chain", "ref": ["suspicious[4].why", "established[4]"], "text": "No official review on disk questions the position.", "t0": 112.47, "t1": 115.11, "shot": "b16", "visual": {"type": "chain", "kicker": "Who decides", "steps": [{"art": "contract", "name": "The agreement", "sub": "crew size and the 5% premium"}, {"art": "van", "name": "Fire Department", "sub": "which trucks are tiller trucks"}, {"art": "magnifier", "name": "Official reviews", "sub": "none on disk questions the position"}]}, "wt": [0.0, 0.18, 0.58, 1.04, 1.21, 1.44, 2.0, 2.1]}, {"scene": "ladders", "kind": "doc", "ref": ["established[3]", "story[4]", "w6", "w7"], "text": "Only two Fire Department files mention wooden ladders:", "t0": 115.33, "t1": 118.58, "shot": "b17", "visual": {"type": "doc", "kicker": "Fire Department Strategic Plan, November 2017", "text": "wooden ladder repair and construction among the services Central Shops provides", "mark": "wooden ladder repair"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.34, 0.67, 0.94, 1.36, 1.78, 2.07, 2.31]}, {"scene": "ladders", "kind": "doc", "ref": ["established[3]", "story[4]", "w6", "w7"], "text": "a 2017 repair service at Central Shops, and a ceremonial ladder raise in 2016.", "t0": 118.58, "t1": 123.63, "shot": "b17", "visual": {"type": "doc", "kicker": "Fire Department Strategic Plan, November 2017", "text": "wooden ladder repair and construction among the services Central Shops provides", "mark": "wooden ladder repair"}, "wt": [0.04, 0.14, 0.39, 0.8, 1.18, 1.52, 1.63, 1.95, 2.76, 2.9, 2.98, 3.54, 3.8, 4.1, 4.2, 4.46]}, {"scene": "close", "kind": "unknowns", "ref": ["notEstablished[0]", "notEstablished[1]", "notEstablished[2]"], "text": "Not shown: that any rule or position is unnecessary, or what the crew rule costs.", "t0": 123.85, "t1": 128.92, "shot": "b18", "visual": {"type": "unknowns", "cards": ["That any crew rule, station or position is unnecessary", "How much of the overtime the crew rule itself causes", "The current daily minimum: the 297 figure is from 2014"]}, "wt": [0.0, 0.32, 1.15, 1.34, 1.53, 1.82, 1.96, 2.38, 2.51, 3.63, 3.74, 3.88, 3.97, 4.23, 4.49]}, {"scene": "close", "kind": "settle", "ref": ["next[0]", "next[4]", "story[5]"], "text": "What would settle it? Overtime by reason code, and a current review of crew size.", "t0": 129.04, "t1": 133.73, "shot": "b19", "visual": {"type": "settle", "cards": [{"who": "", "what": "Overtime of the crew ranks by reason code"}, {"who": "", "what": "Any review of truck crew size or the daily minimum after 2014"}], "focus": 0}, "wt": [0.0, 0.14, 0.34, 0.64, 1.24, 1.77, 1.96, 2.3, 2.92, 3.09, 3.16, 3.49, 3.88, 3.98, 4.21]}, {"scene": "close", "kind": "status", "ref": ["status", "innocent[4]", "defense[0]"], "text": "The City agreed these rules, and voters adopted Proposition F. No one is accused here.", "t0": 133.85, "t1": 139.57, "shot": "b20", "visual": {"type": "status"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.17, 0.47, 0.85, 1.11, 1.62, 1.82, 2.23, 2.63, 3.24, 4.41, 4.67, 4.84, 4.96, 5.4]}, {"scene": "close", "kind": "end", "ref": ["end"], "text": "A lead is a question, not an accusation.", "t0": 139.69, "t1": 141.79, "shot": "b21", "visual": {"type": "end"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.11, 0.31, 0.4, 0.47, 1.18, 1.36, 1.45]}], "format": 6, "chapters": {"open": "Ladders and drivers", "lead1": "Lead 1 · crews in the agreement", "lead2": "Lead 2 · locked into place", "lead3": "Lead 3 · five on a truck", "lead4": "Lead 4 · the overtime", "lead5": "Lead 5 · the tiller operator", "ladders": "The wooden ladders", "close": "Where it stands"}, "look": "midnight", "hook": "question"}